You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S05
Scenario title: Specification Document Review
Initial workflow description:
An engineer reviews a specification document to check whether new features are reflected correctly and whether there are typos or missing details.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or condition starts the review process — for example, is it triggered automatically when a new document version is submitted, or does someone manually assign the review task to the engineer?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "In what system and format is the specification document stored and accessed by the reviewer — for instance, a document management platform, version control repository, or email, and is the document structured or free-form text?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Does the engineer follow a defined checklist or set of criteria when reviewing the document, or is the review based on personal judgment and experience?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Besides the reviewing engineer, are there other roles involved in this workflow — such as a document author who receives feedback, a team lead who gives final approval, or a quality assurance role?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What are the possible outcomes at the end of the review, and what action is taken for each outcome — for example, if issues are found, is the document sent back for revision, and if it passes, who is notified and what happens next?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "How does the engineer record and communicate the issues found during the review — for example, are comments added directly in the document, logged in a separate tracking tool, or sent via email — and how is resolution of those issues confirmed?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Review a specification document for feature coverage, consistency, and editorial errors.",
  "actors": [
    "document reviewer",
    "feature owner",
    "document author",
    "approver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "document repository",
    "change request tracker",
    "review checklist",
    "commenting tool"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "specification document",
    "feature change list",
    "previous document version",
    "review checklist"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "review comments",
    "change request list",
    "approval decision",
    "updated document"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect document and related change list",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Compare feature changes with document content",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Check terminology and formatting consistency",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Record comments and requested revisions",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Revise document based on comments",
      "actor": "document author"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Confirm revisions with feature owner",
      "actor": "feature owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Approve final document",
      "actor": "approver"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are all feature changes reflected?",
      "branches": [
        "complete",
        "missing changes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Are the revisions acceptable?",
      "branches": [
        "approve",
        "request another revision"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing change list",
    "conflicting terminology",
    "unclear feature owner",
    "unresolved comments"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Feature coverage can be checked by comparing change lists and document sections."
    },
    {
      "target": "A3",
      "rationale": "Terminology, formatting, and typo checks can be automated."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Review comments can be grouped by section, severity, and owner."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}

Additional constraint for this respondent: convey the same information as above, but do not reuse the
reference workflow's wording. Rephrase every activity, system, artifact, actor and condition in your own
words while preserving the meaning. Do not copy reference phrases verbatim.
